---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "THCA (Tetrahydrocannabinolic Acid)"
letter: "T"
anchor: "thca"
category: "cannabinoids"
---

The raw, non-intoxicating precursor to THC found in unheated cannabis. Raw cannabis flower contains mostly THCA, not THC. Decarboxylation — applying heat — converts THCA to active THC. Eating raw cannabis produces no intoxicating effect because THCA doesn't bind to CB1 receptors the way THC does. This is why decarboxylation is a non-negotiable first step in any edibles process.

→ [How to Decarb Cannabis](/edibles/decarb-activate-cannabis-edibles/), [What Is THC?](/cannabis-101/what-is-thc/)
